 ```

+#### signal
+
+Type: `AbortSignal`
+
+Cancel queued (not yet started) tasks when the signal is aborted. Pending promises are rejected with the signal's abort reason.
+
+Note: This does not cancel tasks that are already running.
+
+Unlike `clearQueue()`, pending tasks are always rejected when using `signal`, regardless of `rejectOnClear`.
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 1, signal: controller.signal});
+
+const promise = limit(() => doSomething());
+
+// Cancels any tasks still waiting in the queue
+controller.abort();
+```
+
 ### limit(fn, ...args)

 Returns the promise returned by calling `fn(...args)`.
